---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import ReviewNotice from '../components/ReviewNotice.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of use | TGM Group"
  description="The terms on which the TGM Group website is made available, and the relationship between this website and any engagement agreement."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Terms', href: '/terms/' }])]}
>
  <PageHero
    accent="navy"
    title="Terms of use"
    lead="The terms on which this website is made available. These govern the website only — the terms of any actual engagement live in a separate signed agreement."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="prose">
        <ReviewNotice>
          The ECTA disclosure block in particular needs the registration number
          and physical address before it is complete, and the limitation of
          liability needs an attorney's eye.
        </ReviewNotice>

        <h2>Who operates this website</h2>
        <p>
          This website is operated by {site.name}. Section 43 of the Electronic
          Communications and Transactions Act requires the following
          disclosures:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Registered name:</strong> {site.legalName}
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Registration number:</strong>
            <span class="placeholder">[Registration number]</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Physical address:</strong>
            <span class="placeholder">[Registered address]</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Email:</strong>
            <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Telephone:</strong>
            <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Directors / members:</strong>
            <span class="placeholder">[Names]</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>This website is not an offer</h2>
        <p>
          Everything on this site is general information about what we do. It is
          not professional advice, it is not an offer capable of acceptance, and
          nothing on it creates a contractual relationship between us.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any engagement between {site.name} and a client is governed by a
          separate written agreement setting out scope, fees, timelines and
          deliverables. Where this website and that agreement differ, the
          agreement applies.
        </p>

        <h2>Accuracy</h2>
        <p>
          We take care that what is published here is accurate at the time of
          publication, and we correct errors when we find them. We do not
          warrant that the site is free of error or that it will always be
          available.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any figures describing past results name the client, the sector and
          the period they were measured over. They describe what happened in
          that engagement. They are not a prediction of what will happen in
          yours.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The content, design, wordmark and visual system on this site belong to
          {site.name} unless stated otherwise. You may read, print and share
          pages for your own non-commercial purposes. You may not republish,
          resell or pass off the material as your own.
        </p>

        <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
        <p>
          Where we link to another site, we do so because it was useful at the
          time. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their
          content or their privacy practices.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          <span class="placeholder">[Attorney to draft]</span> — this clause
          should be written specifically for {site.name} rather than copied from
          another site. A limitation of liability that is too broad is
          unenforceable under South African consumer protection law, and one
          that is absent leaves the business exposed.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of South Africa,
          and the South African courts have jurisdiction.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms:
          <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Last updated:</strong>
          <span class="placeholder">[Date of legal sign-off]</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
